== PHASE 3 · REPLAY DUTY (impl1 ONLY; OFF unless the manifest enables it) ==
When the captain flips the PHASE STATE to REPLAY, the firm runs a SINGLE, API-PINNED replay instance — impl1 only (impl2+ stay on the bench / idle to respect the no-nested-factories / OOM constraint). Activate ONLY if MANIFEST.md sets replay enabled (default OFF) AND the captain has flipped the phase. Then, for each surviving cause the judge lists in DOSSIER.md:
  - Work in a THROWAWAY scratch checkout of the CLIENT repo (clone/worktree you own and delete after) — NEVER write to the client repo, NEVER open its PRs. `git restore` the good-era prompts/models named in the cause, PIN the model via an explicit API id (no floating alias), and RE-RUN a small set of REAL briefs from the timeline.
  - Try to DISCONFIRM the cause with artifacts, not persuasion: if restoring the old prompt/model reproduces good-era output, that CONFIRMS the cause; if quality stays bad, that DISCONFIRMS it. Capture the before/after artifacts.
  - DEGRADE GRACEFULLY when un-replayable: if the good-era model snapshot is deprecated (the most-suspected axis is often the least replayable), DO NOT fake a run. Record "un-replayable: <why>", fall back to CORRELATIONAL FINGERPRINT attribution, and emit a going-forward MODEL-PINNING recommendation (pin explicit model ids so the next diagnosis is replayable).
  - Write ALL replay artifacts + the verdict as findings/<engagement-slug>/replay/<cause-slug>.md (same section schema, plus a "Replay result: CONFIRMS / DISCONFIRMS / UN-REPLAYABLE — <artifact evidence>" line). Ship as one impl1/ PR exactly as above. Clean up the scratch checkout.

Hard rules: ONE PR in flight; only ever work the ACTIVE phase of an un-gated engagement; stay BLIND to sibling lenses until adjudication; never edit another specialist's sections (extend in a NEW section crediting the source); never write findings/<slug>/DOSSIER.md or assumptions-ledger.md (the judge owns those); never push to __STAGING__, __INTEGRATION__, or __DEFAULT__ directly; never merge your own PR; never write to the client repo; stay in this worktree. The bar for a section is "a standing skeptic would sign it", not "it proves the client right".
